     <h1>Exercise Name: Standing Mid-Cable Fly / Cable Crossover</h1>
     <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>
This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates Standing Mid-Cable Chest Crossovers (Middle Cable Flyes). The video highlights how adjusting the pulleys to chest height aligns the cable resistance directly with the middle chest muscle fibers (Pectoralis Major), maximizing tension right across the sternal head.
 Exercise Name: Standing Mid-Cable Fly / Cable Crossover
 Target Muscles: Middle Chest (Pectoralis Major — Sternal Head)
 Secondary Muscles: Anterior Deltoids (front shoulders), Core (for stability)

</div></dvi>
<pre>
<h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1><u><h4><b>1. Setup</b></h4></u>
 Set both pulley handles on a dual cable machine at chest height. Grab a handle in each hand, step forward to pull the weights off the stack, and place one foot forward for balance.
 <u><h4><b>2. Arm Position</b></h4></u>
 Stand tall with your chest up and shoulders back. Keep a soft, slight bend in your elbows throughout the entire movement.
 <u><h4><b>3. Fly Phase (Concentric)</b></h4></u>
 Exhale as you bring your hands together directly in front of your chest in a sweeping hugging arc until your hands meet or slightly cross.
 <u><h4><b>4. Peak Squeeze</b></h4></u>
 Pause for a split second at the center, squeezing your middle chest as hard as possible.
 Return Phase (Eccentric): Inhale as you slowly allow the cables to pull your hands back to the starting position until you feel a comfortable stretch in your pecs.


<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Direct Cable Alignment:</b> Cable resistance pulls directly inline with the middle pectoral muscle fibers for optimal biomechanical efficiency.
 <b>◉Constant Tension:</b> Keeps uniform tension on the chest muscles even at the top of the movement, unlike dumbbell flyes.
 <b>◉Core & Postural Stability:</b> Standing execution engages your abdominal core to keep your body anchored against the pull of the cables.



<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Maintain a fixed bend in your elbows so you do not push the cables like a press—focus purely on bringing your upper arms together across your body.
